class.description:
Far away, a tree's thousands of leaves cover a few pixels. An [Impostor] is the tree (or a rock, or a building) baked from many directions over the upper half of a sphere into one texture, and drawn as a single quad turned to the camera showing the view baked nearest its direction: a fraction of the cost, and from far away it looks the same.
Bake it with [method bake] from a node in the scene, in a tool script in the editor (then save it) or as the game loads, and give it to a [Scatter3D]'s [member Scatter3D.impostor], or draw [method get_mesh] yourself (with an [InstanceGroup3D] or a [MultiMeshInstance3D] past a visibility range).
[codeblock]
var impostor := Impostor.new()
var result: Dictionary = await impostor.bake($Oak)
if result.ok:
    ResourceSaver.save(impostor, "res://trees/oak_impostor.res")
[/codeblock]
